      statement:
        "<p>It's 09:20 on a Tuesday. An app team escalates: their RHEL 9 API servers are 'slow', p99 is 15x normal, and their dashboard shows load average at 40 on 8-vCPU machines. You SSH in: <code>top</code> shows CPU ~90% idle, no obvious hog, memory looks fine. The app team is already proposing a fleet-wide restart 'to clear it'.</p><p>Walk the triage as the senior engineer on the bridge: what load average actually counts on Linux (hint: not just runnable tasks), the decision tree from <code>vmstat</code> through <code>iostat</code>, <code>pidstat</code>, <code>ss</code>, and <code>/proc</code> that localizes the bottleneck in minutes, and how you distinguish the classic culprits — storage latency, NFS hangs, lock contention in the kernel, cgroup throttling. Then the architect part: why the blind restart is worse than doing nothing, what evidence you capture before any mitigation, and what you change so this class of incident pages with a diagnosis attached instead of a mystery.</p>",
